data step_emitter_word_wall_coverage_gap: IntegrationConcern = IntegrationConcern {
  identity: "step_emitter_word_wall_coverage_gap",
  kind: SuspectedCapabilityGap {
    model: decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.gunbc_invoke_step_emit", decl_name: "gunbc_run_step_script"),
    requirement: "the run-step emitter path (gunbc_run_step_script -> gunbc_run_step_intent -> gunbc_invoke_step_emit_pipeline) enforces the invoke word wall on the run-body entry the way gunbc_run_command already does, so a hostile metacharacter entry is refused as a typed, located Diagnostic at the artifact boundary; today only gunbc_run_command crosses the alphabet guard, so attacker-shaped text admitted on the step-emitter path reaches committed workflow shell as a passing step",
    standing: RequirementEstablished { by: step_emitter_word_wall_coverage_gap_review },
  },
  affected: FreeSemigroup {
    head: decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.gunbc_invoke_step_emit", decl_name: "gunbc_run_step_script"),
    tail: [
      decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.gunbc_invoke_step_emit", decl_name: "gunbc_run_step_intent"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.gunbc_invoke_step_emit", decl_name: "gunbc_invoke_step_emit_pipeline"),
    ],
  },
  question: "does the step-emitter path enforce the invoke word wall? It does not -- only gunbc_run_command crosses the alphabet guard, so gunbc_invoke_word_wall_refuses_metacharacter_entry_holds is red on the origin/main tip AND on the head that retyped the emitter (identical red, not a regression from the retype). When the step-emitter path is brought behind the same word wall that gunbc_invoke_word_wall_diagnostic already emits (the alphabet guard applied to the run-body entry), the witness turns green and this row closes.",
  sightings: FreeSemigroup {
    head: ConcernSighting {
      revision: "f945b1575d5df3c7f3ed0155a5c53675f23341d6",
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.gunbc_invoke_step_emit", decl_name: "gunbc_invoke_step_emit_pipeline") },
        tail: [
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.gunbc_invoke_witness", decl_name: "gunbc_invoke_word_wall_refuses_metacharacter_entry_holds") },
        ],
      },
      account: "Recorded while integrating emitter_string_return_carries_no_typed_refusal (review 97776). The retype deleted the three __GUNBC_INVOKE_EMIT_REFUSED__ poisons + the tier_o_workflow_produced scan, but the retained red control gunbc_invoke_word_wall_refuses_metacharacter_entry_holds was left red with no owner -- 'owned elsewhere' named no row, an untracked stall (gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder meta-obligation 2). The discriminator is red on the origin/main tip and on this head alike: the step-emitter path never crosses the word wall, only gunbc_run_command does, so a metacharacter entry is admitted. Deliberately NOT fixed here (out of scope for the invoke-emitter retype; the fix is a word-wall application at the run-body entry, its own change). Recorded so the class is tracked and names its next-rung trigger, per gunbc.design_argument::continuous_generalization ('an unfinished reconciliation is recorded, not remembered').",
    },
    tail: [],
  },
  disposition: Open,
